<https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/occupation/OCC0022> a seom:Occupation ;
    rdfs:label "Asbestos analyst and surveyor" ;
    dct:description "Asbestos is a hazardous material that is present within many buildings in the UK and past exposure currently results in 5000 deaths per year. Asbestos Analysts and Surveyors perform an essential role in the identification, analysis and monitoring of asbestos materials by assisting employers and property owners in understanding the risks asbestos presents and advising on how to control these risks. This occupational role is essential in order to ensure employers comply with the legal duties placed on them. The role involves the inspection of buildings, premises and machinery for the presence of asbestos materials as well as the assessment of identified materials and the provision of information to employers to allow them to manage the risks the asbestos may present. The widespread nature of asbestos means visiting a wide range of building types including schools, offices, factories and homes. In addition to this, the role will involve the monitoring and management of asbestos removal operations. To ensure no conflict of interest the surveyor role does not involve removal work, which must be carried out by an independent organisation. The surveyor will assess the presence of asbestos and identify where levels are such that they require removal action to take place. Removal contractors will carry out the removal and an independent surveyor will carry out final checks before the building is returned to the owner. The occupation involves working in a highly-controlled environment with all works being undertaken in accordance with strict regulatory guidelines, enforced by the Health and Safety Executive (HSE) and meeting the technical requirements of the United Kingdom Accreditation Service (UKAS)." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Asbestos analyst and surveyor" ;
    seom:atTechnicalLevel <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/technical-level/1> ;
    seom:deliveredThrough <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/product/ST0022> ;
    seom:hasStatus <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/status/4> ;
    seom:inCluster <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/cluster/54> ;
    seom:inPathway <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/pathway/27> ;
    seom:inRoute <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/route/5> ;
    seom:involvedEmployers "Thames Laboratories, Clearwater Environmental, Riverside Environmental, Environmental Essentials, Bradley Environmental, DAC Asbestos Limited, Askams, ABP Ltd, Asbestos Testing and Consultancy Association, Lucion" ;
    seom:keyword "Asbestos Analyst/Surveyor",
        "asbestos",
        "asbestos materials",
        "asbestos regulations",
        "asbestos removal operations" ;
    seom:level 3 ;
    seom:overview "Performing an essential role in the identification, analysis and monitoring of asbestos materials." ;
    seom:socMapping2010 <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/soc/2010/3567> ;
    seom:statusLastUpdated "2018-06-29"^^xsd:date ;
    seom:stdCode "OCC0022" ;
    seom:versionNo "1.1" .

