<https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/occupation/OCC0428> a seom:Occupation ;
    rdfs:label "Port marine operations officer" ;
    dct:description "As an island nation over 95% of trade by volume goes by ship through over 100 ports around the United Kingdom. UK ports employ around 118,000 people across a wide range of port types and activities; from container and bulk cargo ports to passenger terminals to leisure and marinas. The port marine operations team assists in ensuring the safe transit and handling of vessels into and out of the port. A Port Marine Operations Officer may work as a leader or member of a port/harbour marine operations team and may be involved in: berthing of vessels, port control and marine services, operation of harbours and marinas, conservancy, environmental protection, statutory compliance and operation of harbour marine craft within the Harbour Authority area of jurisdiction. This is a highly responsible position with a key contribution to the safe and efficient operation of the harbour. The role may involve shift working and working in all environments. Port Operation Officer apprenticeship is designed to give those interested in working in a marine environment the opportunity to learn about shipping and port operations, while working for a port operator. The apprenticeship is designed to give hands-on training in all aspects of port marine operations such as lock and dock operations, mooring boat operations, health and safety task within a port operation, radio room and marine control centre operations as well as role and responsibilities of Berthing Master, Dock Masters and deputies, Harbour Masters and their assistants." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Port marine operations officer" ;
    seom:atTechnicalLevel <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/technical-level/2> ;
    seom:deliveredThrough <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/product/ST0428> ;
    seom:hasStatus <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/status/1> ;
    seom:inCluster <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/cluster/13> ;
    seom:inPathway <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/pathway/11> ;
    seom:inRoute <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/route/15> ;
    seom:involvedEmployers "ABP, Port of Blyth, Port of Tyne, Dover Harbour Board, Port of Tilbury, Shoreham Port, Port Of London, Bristol Ports, Pool Harbour Commision, Peel Ports" ;
    seom:keyword "marine environment",
        "marine operations",
        "port",
        "transport",
        "vessel" ;
    seom:level 4 ;
    seom:overview "Assists in ensuring the safe transit and handling of vessels into and out of the port." ;
    seom:progressesTo <https://gov.tesseract.academy/id/seom/occupation/OCC0427>,
